repo goyek/goyek\\n\\nResolved tag v2.3.0 to sha1:580d400496e680ca42e42e5101f591dc1e6a747c\\n\\nLoaded attestation from GitHub API\\n\\n✓ Release v2.3.0 verified!\\n\\n```\\n\\n> [!CAUTION]\\n\\n> It is not possible to add/edit/remove release assets (artifacts) after the release is published. \\n\\n> This is great, but maybe some repositories add the assets after the release is already published. The release process must be checked for the repositories before enabling the feature.\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\n> This command cannot be used to verify the source code zip file or tarball for a release, since these assets are only created when a download is requested.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 03 issu recommend immut releas open telemetri sig secur 164 canon url http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 author trask creat 2025 08 27t13 31 30z updat 2026 01 28t22 16 50z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label mileston descript http github blog changelog 2025 08 26 releas now support immut in public preview sourc id src issu 03 issu recommend immut releas open telemetri sig secur 164 canon url http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 author trask creat 2025 08 27t13 31 30z updat 2026 01 28t22 16 50z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label mileston discuss 9 pellar 2025 09 16t12 52 39z i test it on my side project check http github com goyek goyek releas tag v2 3 0 and notic the immut text and icon a well a releas attest json in the releas asset test gh releas verifi v2 3 0 repo goyek goyek resolv tag v2 3 0 to sha1 580d400496e680ca42e42e5101f591dc1e6a747c load attest from github api releas v2 3 0 verifi caution it is not possibl to add edit remov releas asset artifact after the releas is publish this is great but mayb some repositori add the asset after the releas is alreadi publish the releas process must be check for the repositori befor enabl the featur import this command can not be use to verifi the sourc code zip file or tarbal for a releas sinc these asset are onli creat when a download is request\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"850c33a1966bb99c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36237075646843625, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17571600924062325, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7978985, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- 2026-01-28T11:30:57Z · **cross-referenced** by pellared ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/pull/219\\n\\n- 2026-01-28T22:16:50Z · **closed** by reyang\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 01 28t11 30 57z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri sig secur pull 219 2026 01 28t22 16 50z close by reyang\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"e62fb3818dcae1f1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32454478365167366, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13213388807381957, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77350354, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Meeting notes: [Ecosystem Explorer Project](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QBpFmSR54fGus8q6RraUj0-mEjSoX7S7fdlgsvxZsuk/edit?usp=sharing)  \\n\\n  - [https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml](https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml)  \\n\\n### SIG Security: release signing\\n\\n- Robert proposed enabling GitHub “signature releases” in addition to existing tag signing and GPG signatures of source archives.\\n\\n- Key points:\\n\\n  - GitHub’s source tarball/zip is generated at download time; signing artifacts strengthens trust and mitigates changes over time.\\n\\n  - Double-signing is acceptable and beneficial for OSS Scorecard/compliance.\\n\\n  - Constraint: Artifacts must be uploaded at release time; cannot regenerate later.\\n\\n- Decision: Proceed with enabling signature releases; update release documentation and ensure process discipline.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164)  \\n\\n### KubeCon updates\\n\\n- OpenTelemetry Observatory booth confirmed.\\n\\n- Go SIG will meet at the booth (Tuesday morning, local time; check published schedule).\\n\\n- Plan to cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; reminder will be sent next week.\\n\\n- Community encouraged to stop by the booth and participate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"meet note ecosystem explor project http doc googl com document d 1qbpfmsr54fgus8q6rrauj0 mejsox7s7fdlgsvxzsuk edit usp share http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml sig secur releas sign robert propos enabl github signatur releas in addit to exist tag sign and gpg signatur of sourc archiv key point github s sourc tarbal zip is generat at download time sign artifact strengthen trust and mitig chang over time doubl sign is accept and benefici for os scorecard complianc constraint artifact must be upload at releas time can not regener later decis proceed with enabl signatur releas updat releas document and ensur process disciplin refer http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 kubecon updat opentelemetri observatori booth confirm go sig will meet at the booth tuesday morn local time check publish schedul plan to cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week remind will be sent next week communiti encourag to stop by the booth and particip sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"0032f870da180d9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3068202174162062, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14506286059458032, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68425405, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Docs:\\n\\n- https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/immutable-releases\\n\\n- https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/preventing-changes-to-your-releases\\n\\n- https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/verifying-the-integrity-of-a-release\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-09-17T18:01:37Z\\n\\nI also checked with my other side-project where releases are done by a GitHub workflow: https://github.com/golang-templates/seed/releases/tag/v0.22.0 where there also some assets:\\n\\n```\\n\\n$ gh release verify v0.22.0 --repo golang-templates/seed\\n\\nResolved tag v0.22.0 to sha1:530c65eeab67c878796dfe194057b7c475f8b9ae\\n\\nLoaded attestation from GitHub API\\n\\n✓ Release v0.22.0 verif