as download v0 22 0 seed _ 0 22 0 _ linux _ amd64 tar gz gh releas verifi asset v0 22 0 seed _ 0 22 0 _ linux _ amd64 tar gz repo golang templat seed\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"30e4ee9202e6d909\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29780153314562485, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10521802163660696, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74716306, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-03]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3390010099  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T13:10:44Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T14:04:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-09\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n## Agenda Items\\n\\n### 1. Milestone Progress Review\\n\\n**Current milestone status:**\\n\\n- 17 items still open in the milestone\\n\\n- Most PRs are in review phase or awaiting final approvals\\n\\n**Key items discussed:**\\n\\n#### Expose temporality selector functions\\n\\n- **Status:** Under discussion, may not be accepted in current form\\n\\n- **Discussion:** Tyler and David discussed whether to expose temporality selector parsing functions for configuration\\n\\n- **Decision:** Not recommended for inclusion in SDK. Users should use full OpenTelemetry configuration file format instead of custom configuration snippets\\n\\n- **Rationale:** Want to standardize on OTel configuration format rather than supporting fragmented approaches\\n\\n- **Action:** Tyler to respond with feedback about standardization preference\\n\\n#### Prometheus Exporter Migration\\n\\n- **Status:** Implementation complete, needs deprecation decision\\n\\n- **Discussion:** Need to decide on deprecating existing configuration options\\n\\n- **Decision:** Tyler supports deprecation before marking as stable\\n\\n- **Next steps:** Handle in next milestone\\n\\n#### Error Handling for Prometheus\\n\\n- **Status:** PR ready for review, waiting for conversation resolution\\n\\n- **Action:** David to review and potentially merge\\n\\n#### High mutex contention in metric sums\\n\\n- **Status:** Resolved via PR #7427\\n\\n- **Action:** Close issue\\n\\n### 2. Optimization Work Discussion\\n\\n**David's current work:**\\n\\n- Implementing lockless exponential histogram\\n\\n- Fun and challenging optimization project\\n\\n- Building on previous optimization PRs\\n\\n**PR Reviews needed:**\\n\\n- **PR #7474:** Exemplar reservoir optimization (approved by Tyler, needs second approval)\\n\\n- **PR #7443:** Histogram optimization (needs review, has race condition issue identified)\\n\\n**Technical discussion on PR #7443:**\\n\\n- Tyler identified potential race condition in min/max tracking with `isSet` flag\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 03 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3390010099 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t13 10 44z updat 2025 10 10t14 04 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 09 attende tyler yahn david ashpol bryan boreham agenda item 1 mileston progress review current mileston status 17 item still open in the mileston most pr are in review phase or await final approv key item discuss expos tempor selector function status under discuss may not be accept in current form discuss tyler and david discuss whether to expos tempor selector pars function for configur decis not recommend for inclus in sdk user should use full opentelemetri configur file format instead of custom configur snippet rational want to standard on otel configur format rather than support fragment approach action tyler to respond with feedback about standard prefer prometheus export migrat status implement complet need deprec decis discuss need to decid on deprec exist configur option decis tyler support deprec befor mark a stabl next step handl in next mileston error handl for prometheus status pr readi for review wait for convers resolut action david to review and potenti merg high mutex content in metric sum status resolv via pr 7427 action close issu 2 optim work discuss david s current work implement lockless exponenti histogram fun and challeng optim project build on previous optim pr pr review need pr 7474 exemplar reservoir optim approv by tyler need second approv pr 7443 histogram optim need review ha race condit issu identifi technic discuss on pr 7443 tyler identifi potenti race condit in min max track with isset flag\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"87365f6e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"id\": \"22374080d99b56a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29629957845349825, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12515724064785463, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6956317, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"87365f6e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3423, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:31\", \"token_count\": 796, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Calculated digest for seed_0.22.0_linux_amd64.tar.gz: sha256:1dfa16bc64b1c8bc76ad5a1da6aed4ed0d9ddb11fe51bfe81e0707d8bd0acbe7\\n\\nResolved tag v0.22.0 to sha1:530c65eeab67c878796dfe194057b7c475f8b9ae\\n\\nLoaded attestation from GitHub API\\n\\n✓ Verification succeeded! seed_0.22.0_linux_amd64.tar.gz is present in release v0.22.0\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-10-14T14:58:10Z\\n\\nRelated issue: https://github.com/ossf/scorecard/issues/4823\\n\\n---\\n\\n**trask** — 2025-10-23T02:38:58Z\\n\\n> as well as \\\"Release attestation (json)\\\" in the release assets\\n\\nDoes this replace the need to attest individual artifacts, e.g. #79?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-10-27T09:21:42Z\\n\\n> > as well as \\\"Release attestation (json)\\\" in the release assets\\n\\n> \\n\\n> Does this replace the need to attest individual artifacts, e.g. [#79](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/79)?\\n\\nI think it can replace it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-11-03T10:38:17Z\\n\\nPreparing OTel Go for enabling the immutable releases:\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7567\\n\\nEDIT: Merged. We are ready for enabling imutable released for https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go and https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib\\n\\nRelated:\\n\\n- https://github.com/integrations/terraform-provider-github/issues/2746\\n\\n@trask, is it a blocker?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**trask** — 2025-11-07T00:20:03Z\\n\\n> @trask, is it a blocker?\\n\\nit doesn't need to block, let's do something like this: https://github.com/open-telemetry/admin/pull/346\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-12-11T17:43:19Z\\n\\nI can confirm that it worked for Go (https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/releases/tag/v1.39.0) and Go Contrib (https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/releases/tag/v1.39.0).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"calcul digest for seed _ 0 22 0 _ linux _ amd64 tar gz sha256 1dfa16bc64b1c8bc76ad5a1da6aed4ed0d9ddb11fe51bfe81e0707d8bd0acbe7 resolv tag v0 22 0 to sha1 530c65eeab67c878796dfe194057b7c475f8b9ae load attest from github api verif succeed seed _ 0 22 0 _ linux _ amd64 tar gz is present in releas v0 22 0 pellar 2025 10 14t14 58 10z relat issu http github com ossf scorecard issu 4823 trask 2025 10 23t02 38 58z a well a releas attest json in the releas asset doe this replac the need to attest individu artifact e g 79 pellar 2025 10 27t09 21 42z a well a releas attest json in the releas asset doe this replac the need to attest individu artifact e g 79 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 79 i think it can replac it pellar 2025 11 03t10 38 17z prepar otel go for enabl the immut releas http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7567 edit merg we are readi for enabl imut releas for http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go and http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib relat http github com integr terraform provid github issu 2746 trask is it a blocker trask 2025 11 07t00 20 03z trask is it a blocker it doesn t need to block let s do someth like this http github com open telemetri admin pull 346 pellar 2025 12 11t17 43 19z i can confirm that it work for go http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go releas tag v1 39 0 and go contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib releas tag v1 39 0\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"85135205c17775f5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2957231652143761, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0903380074491087, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7749552, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Can you share more about why you aren't able to migrate to the stats handler?  We [deprecated](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/4534) the interceptors almost 2 years ago, which seems like plenty of time to migrate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-28T20:40:37Z\\n\\nEven if we removed all of our references, references in transitive dependencies still cause compilation errors, and we don’t have control over the timeline at which transitive dependencies remove those code references.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-29T08:35:31Z\\n\\nThat doesn't look like a good reason to me. There will always be unmaintained transitive dependencies that prevent this kind of upgrades.\\n\\nThat's tech debt that needs to be fixed, not kept on our end.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T16:28:55Z\\n\\nThe question is really whether we can rely on otelgrpc to be stable! For now, we are stuck on v0.58.0 because of compilation errors on higher versions introduced by the breaking change. If there is an urgent security patch introduced, we won’t be able to upgrade to it.\\n\\nGenerally, with Golang, we avoid breaking changes aggressively avoid these kinds of things. Does maintaining this interceptor involve significant overhead from the maintainers?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T17:37:26Z\\n\\nPlease do not rely on an unstable package as being stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T17:38:42Z\\n\\nAre there plans to make this package stable? Or are we sticking with [ZeroVer](https://0ver.org/) for the forseeable future?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T18:06:47Z\\n\\n> Are there plans to make this package stable?\\n\\nThere is definitely desire among project contributor to progress this package towards stability. But please understand this is an open-source project. It is driven by a the dedicated effort of engineers who donate their time to working on this. That time is valuable and allocated to many efforts.\\n\\nI'm happy to add the question of stabilization to our weekly SIG meeting happening tomorrow. @nicholasngai I would strongly suggest you attend the meeting tomorrow to discuss your use-case and help motivate allocation of effort for this stabilization. I don't anticipate this stabilization happening within 2025, but I could see us prioritizing it for 2026 if we have community involvement and/or added developer help here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"can you share more about whi you aren t abl to migrat to the stat handler we deprec http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 4534 the interceptor almost 2 year ago which seem like plenti of time to migrat nicholasngai 2025 10 28t20 40 37z even if we remov all of our refer refer in transit depend still caus compil error and we don t have control over the timelin at which transit depend remov those code refer dmathieu 2025 10 29t08 35 31z that doesn t look like a good reason to me there will alway be unmaintain transit depend that prevent this kind of upgrad that s tech debt that need to be fix not kept on our end nicholasngai 2025 10 29t16 28 55z the question is realli whether we can reli on otelgrpc to be stabl for now we are stuck on v0 580 becaus of compil error on higher version introduc by the break chang if there is an urgent secur patch introduc we won t be abl to upgrad to it general with golang we avoid break chang aggress avoid these kind of thing doe maintain this interceptor involv signific overhead from the maintain mralia 2025 10 29t17 37 26z pleas do not reli on an unstabl packag a be stabl nicholasngai 2025 10 29t17 38 42z are there plan to make this packag stabl or are we stick with zerov http 0ver org for the forseeabl futur mralia 2025 10 29t18 06 47z are there plan to make this packag stabl there is definit desir among project contributor to progress this packag toward stabil but pleas understand this is an open sourc project it is driven by a the dedic effort of engin who donat their time to work on this that time is valuabl and alloc to mani effort i m happi to add the question of stabil to our week sig meet happen tomorrow nicholasngai i would strong suggest you attend the meet tomorrow to discus your use case and help motiv alloc of effort for this stabil i don t anticip this stabil happen within 2025 but i could see u priorit it for 2026 if we have communiti involv and or ad develop help here\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"id\": \"1afc8125e2debda9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2671658035705273, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08147591938646763, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7004422, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4910, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:12\", \"token_count\": 1517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Two non-observability items noted:\\n\\n  - Sync map / atomics for fixed bucket histograms.\\n\\n  - Exemplar reservoir changes.\\n\\n- Safe to slip to next release; include if ready.\\n\\n### 4. Stabilizing new attribute value types\\n\\n- Discussion about stabilizing new spec attribute types (byte arrays, “any” type).\\n\\n- Prototype implementation exists and needs review.\\n\\n- Considered tricky; careful review needed around limits and types.\\n\\n### 5. Processor `Enabled` method\\n\\n- Proposal from Robert to move `Enabled` from filter processor to main processor interface.\\n\\n- Spec now stabilized and allows this.\\n\\n- Pros: consistent API, less ad-hoc type assertion/boilerplate in docs.\\n\\n- Con: processors that are “always enabled” need a trivial `Enabled() bool { return true }`.\\n\\n- General agreement; will revisit for final confirmation.\\n\\n### 6. OTLP `insecure` support (logs, env vars, spec)\\n\\n- PR adds `insecure` (env var) support for OTLP **logs**, matching traces/metrics.\\n\\n- HTTP OTLP config historically messy; env vars common in practice.\\n\\n- Spec unclear due to moratorium on env vars.\\n\\n- Direction: add logs support in Go; push for spec clarity later.\\n\\n### 7. Collector protobuf changes & PDataGen\\n\\n- Collector removed dependency on Go protobuf types; now uses `pdataGen`.\\n\\n- Large internal rewrite; significant line count reduction.\\n\\n- Benchmarks improved (fewer allocations).\\n\\n- Some cross-language quirks surfaced but manageable.\\n\\n- Go SIG interested in exploring similar approaches; needs more benchmarking.\\n\\n### 8. KubeCon & talks\\n\\n- First SIG meeting since KubeCon.\\n\\n- Members encouraged to share notable talks and videos once available.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Merge OTelConf RC support PR as-is (pending normal review).\\n\\n- Track experimental API structure review (e.g., `x` submodule) under the `1.40.0` milestone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"two non observ item note sync map atom for fix bucket histogram exemplar reservoir chang safe to slip to next releas includ if readi 4 stabil new attribut valu type discuss about stabil new spec attribut type byte array ani type prototyp implement exist and need review consid tricki care review need around limit and type 5 processor enabl method propos from robert to move enabl from filter processor to main processor interfac spec now stabil and allow this pro consist api less ad hoc type assert boilerpl in doc con processor that are alway enabl need a trivial enabl bool return true general agreement will revisit for final confirm 6 otlp insecur support log env var spec pr add insecur env var support for otlp log match trace metric http otlp config histor messi env var common in practic spec unclear due to moratorium on env var direct add log support in go push for spec clariti later 7 collector protobuf chang pdatagen collector remov depend on go protobuf type now us pdatagen larg intern rewrit signific line count reduct benchmark improv fewer alloc some cross languag quirk surfac but manag go sig interest in explor similar approach need more benchmark 8 kubecon talk first sig 